   "shortTitle": "Energy controls the covering radius",
   "figures": [],
   "summaryHtml": "<p>The argument bounding the covering radius <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"R(X)\"></span> by the quantization energy, <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\mathscr F\\ge cR^4\"></span> in two dimensions <a class=\"ref ref-eq\" href=\"#eq/eq:F_vs_R\" data-label=\"eq:F_vs_R\">(4.15)</a>, is inspired by [<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#bib/KriegSonnleitner2024\" data-key=\"KriegSonnleitner2024\" title=\"David Krieg and Mathias Sonnleitner. Random points are optimal for the approximation of Sobolev functions. IMA Journal of Numerical Analysis, 44(3):1346–1371, 2024.\">24</a>, Section 2.5] and [<a class=\"cite\" href=\"#bib/ElNmeirLuschgyPages2022\" data-key=\"ElNmeirLuschgyPages2022\" title=\"Rancy El Nmeir, Harald Luschgy, and Gilles Pagès. New approach to greedy vector quantization. Bernoulli, 28(1):424–452, 2022.\">13</a>, proof of Proposition 2.1].</p>",
